WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.531
An industrial control system combines people, procedures, hardware, software, and networks to monitor and control a physical process.

00:00:09.531 --> 00:00:13.686
Field devices measure conditions and perform actions.

00:00:13.686 --> 00:00:15.885
Controllers execute logic.

00:00:15.885 --> 00:00:21.506
HMIs and SCADA platforms give operators visibility and supervisory control.

00:00:21.506 --> 00:00:29.571
Engineering workstations hold privileged configuration and programming capabilities, while historians preserve process evidence over time.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:41.545
Industrial networks connect these functions through Ethernet, serial, wireless, and specialized protocols whose timing and availability requirements may differ from ordinary enterprise traffic.

00:00:41.545 --> 00:00:48.633
Architecture models help teams understand the field, control, supervisory, operations, and enterprise relationships.

00:00:48.633 --> 00:01:03.540
The Purdue model is a useful reference, and an industrial DMZ can mediate necessary exchange, but each organization must document its real systems, data flows, remote paths, and dependencies.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.717
Security depends on process context.

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:16.248
The same technical event can have different consequences depending on equipment state, operational timing, redundancy, and safety design.

00:01:16.248 --> 00:01:25.779
Cybersecurity teams need operators and engineers to interpret evidence and choose actions that do not create additional hazards.

00:01:25.779 --> 00:01:39.220
Strong ICS security protects safety, reliability, availability, and process integrity through accurate inventory, segmentation, controlled access, trusted configuration, passive monitoring, change management, backups, and practiced response.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:52.661
The central lesson is architectural: protect each component according to its operational role and protect the pathways that allow those components to work as a system.
